 is 64\u00b0F (1999). The low of <strong>15\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Record highs and lows, by the decade that set them","p_rec":"If Hibbing's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Hibbing has set <strong>165 standing record lows</strong>, more than the 111 that chance alone would give, and <strong>126 record highs</strong>, close to the 111 that chance alone would give. The 2000s hold the most record highs of any decade (46). Hibbing's all-time high is 98\u00b0F, on July 27, 1988.","t_chg":"Hibbing's nights cooled over the long run. Its days show no clear change.","p_chg":"Across 85 complete years: Hibbing's average low has fallen <strong class='sig'>\u22120.40\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range \u22120.58 to \u22120.22), about \u22123.4\u00b0F since 1939. Hibbing's average high shows no clear change: +0.09\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.07 to +0.25) that includes zero.","t_mon":"Lows rose in none; 7 months fell. Highs rose in 2 of 12 months; October fell.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Hibbing's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.01 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 24.5 inches a year. The wettest year was 1999 (38.64 in); the driest, 2006 (12.14 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 9 daily record highs, 3 daily record lows"}}